<BaseLayout title="About | Evan Hobson" description="About Evan Hobson.">
  <section class="page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I grew interested in modeling because the way a question gets formalized can change the
      answer. My cattle paper is an example: three cheatgrass maps, used in the same model, give
      three different accounts of how cows respond to cheatgrass. I want to work on problems like
      that, where the modeling choices matter to someone managing land.
    </p>

    <p>
      In graduate school I want to keep working in movement ecology, with step-selection and
      behavioral data from biologgers, on questions that come out of working landscapes.
    </p>

    <p>
      My faith shapes why I care about this. I think of land management as stewardship, which means
      acting carefully when we don't fully understand a system and remembering the people who
      depend on it.
    </p>

    <p>
      I am married to Lily. Outside research I am learning jazz piano.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
